WEBVTT

00:00:00.141 --> 00:00:01.815
Here's the rate graph from the end of

00:00:01.855 --> 00:00:02.520
the last video.

00:00:03.343 --> 00:00:05.826
Water flows into this rainwater tank at two

00:00:05.887 --> 00:00:08.310
t times e to the t squared litres

00:00:08.351 --> 00:00:08.811
per second,

00:00:09.513 --> 00:00:11.516
so the graph shows how fast the water

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:13.399
is coming in, not how much is there.

00:00:14.302 --> 00:00:16.467
A question could ask how much water flows

00:00:16.488 --> 00:00:17.651
in during the first second.

00:00:18.295 --> 00:00:19.800
It could ask for the volume at any

00:00:19.861 --> 00:00:20.342
time t.

00:00:21.347 --> 00:00:23.592
Another question could ask for an area, or

00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:25.176
give you only a table of readings.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.326
Every one of those needs an integral, but

00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:29.390
not the same one.

00:00:30.094 --> 00:00:31.959
So how do you tell which integral a

00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:32.742
question needs?

00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:35.099
The first thing to read is what the

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.202
question asks for.

00:00:36.925 --> 00:00:38.367
If it asks for the function itself,

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:41.552
use an indefinite integral, and a known value

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:42.474
fixes the plus C.

00:00:43.277 --> 00:00:45.080
Starting from the known value and adding a

00:00:45.161 --> 00:00:46.404
definite integral works too.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.651
If it asks how much something changes between

00:00:49.712 --> 00:00:50.332
two times,

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.076
use a definite integral.

00:00:52.778 --> 00:00:55.160
A definite integral adds up rate times a

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.123
small time, so it gives the change,

00:00:57.665 --> 00:00:59.807
and parts below the axis count as negative.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.390
If it asks for the area between a

00:01:02.452 --> 00:01:05.234
graph and the axis, or a distance, split

00:01:05.275 --> 00:01:07.437
where the graph crosses zero, and add the

00:01:07.458 --> 00:01:08.818
parts as positive amounts.

00:01:09.662 --> 00:01:11.527
And if it gives you only readings, there's

00:01:11.568 --> 00:01:14.056
no formula to integrate, so estimate with the

00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:14.919
trapezoidal rule.

00:01:15.906 --> 00:01:17.898
Which one does "how much flows in" need?

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:19.587
Think for three seconds.

00:01:20.773 --> 00:01:23.219
It's a change between two times, so it's

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.161
a definite integral.

00:01:24.935 --> 00:01:26.738
So find the integral from zero to one

00:01:27.059 --> 00:01:28.802
of two t, times e to the t

00:01:28.823 --> 00:01:29.203
squared.

00:01:29.987 --> 00:01:30.912
Look inside first.

00:01:31.336 --> 00:01:34.087
The inside is t squared, and its derivative,

00:01:34.169 --> 00:01:35.474
two t, is out the front.

00:01:36.037 --> 00:01:37.783
So a primitive is e to the t

00:01:37.844 --> 00:01:38.184
squared.

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:41.130
At one, that's e, and at zero it's

00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:43.654
one, so the water added is e minus

00:01:43.795 --> 00:01:45.737
one litres, about one point seven two.

00:01:46.741 --> 00:01:48.869
The rate is never negative here, so this

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.617
is also the area under the curve.

00:01:51.301 --> 00:01:53.432
On the tank's gauge, that's the water added

00:01:53.554 --> 00:01:54.458
in the first second.

00:01:55.095 --> 00:01:56.020
Now the second question.

00:01:56.725 --> 00:01:59.044
The tank held five litres at the start.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.093
Find the volume at time t.

00:02:01.977 --> 00:02:04.183
This asks for a function, so use the

00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:05.287
indefinite integral.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.774
V of t is e to the t

00:02:07.815 --> 00:02:09.037
squared, plus C.

00:02:09.821 --> 00:02:12.489
At t equals zero, that's one plus C,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.918
and it has to be five, so C

00:02:15.059 --> 00:02:15.560
is four.

00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:17.967
So V of t is e to the

00:02:18.028 --> 00:02:19.591
t squared, plus four.

00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:21.045
Here's a good check.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.062
V of one minus V of zero is

00:02:24.304 --> 00:02:26.912
e plus four, minus five, which is e

00:02:27.214 --> 00:02:27.815
minus one.

00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:30.382
It's the same amount as before, because the

00:02:30.444 --> 00:02:32.047
C cancels when you subtract.

00:02:32.816 --> 00:02:33.720
Here's a different graph.

00:02:34.504 --> 00:02:36.387
A small boat on a canal moves with

00:02:36.428 --> 00:02:39.532
velocity t squared minus two t metres per

00:02:39.593 --> 00:02:42.056
second, from t equals zero to three.

00:02:42.779 --> 00:02:43.671
How far does it travel?

00:02:44.541 --> 00:02:46.675
The integral from zero to three is zero.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.188
That's the displacement.

00:02:48.551 --> 00:02:50.378
The boat ends exactly where it started.

00:02:51.084 --> 00:02:52.013
But it did move.

00:02:52.782 --> 00:02:55.506
The velocity is negative until t equals two,

00:02:55.888 --> 00:02:58.512
so it drifts back first, then comes forward.

00:02:59.136 --> 00:02:59.921
Split at two.

00:03:00.666 --> 00:03:03.090
The first piece is minus four thirds, and

00:03:03.132 --> 00:03:04.554
the second is four thirds.

00:03:05.157 --> 00:03:07.389
Count both as positive, and the distance is

00:03:07.571 --> 00:03:08.636
eight thirds of a metre.

00:03:09.119 --> 00:03:10.846
Zero is the classic wrong answer here.

00:03:11.803 --> 00:03:12.331
Last kind.

00:03:12.755 --> 00:03:14.919
A different tank's inflow is read every two

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:15.240
minutes:

00:03:15.742 --> 00:03:18.709
three, five, six, four and two litres per

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.914
minute, from t equals zero to eight.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:22.754
Estimate the water added.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.351
There's no formula, so we can't integrate it

00:03:25.452 --> 00:03:25.934
exactly.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.685
Use the trapezoidal rule.

00:03:28.369 --> 00:03:30.975
Each trapezium joins two neighbouring readings with a

00:03:31.036 --> 00:03:31.657
straight line.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.171
The strips are two minutes wide, so h

00:03:34.615 --> 00:03:34.996
is two.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.853
The ends count once, and the inside readings

00:03:37.895 --> 00:03:38.517
count twice.

00:03:39.141 --> 00:03:41.965
That's two over two, times three, plus two

00:03:42.026 --> 00:03:45.190
times fifteen, plus two, which is thirty-five.

00:03:45.772 --> 00:03:47.549
So about thirty-five litres flowed in.

00:03:48.174 --> 00:03:49.878
It's an estimate, because we don't know the

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.002
rate between readings.

00:03:51.669 --> 00:03:52.574
Now a quick sort.

00:03:53.138 --> 00:03:55.470
For each question, decide which kind it is,

00:03:55.571 --> 00:03:56.677
but don't work it out yet.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.446
First, a town's population, in thousands, grows at

00:04:00.588 --> 00:04:02.932
three e to the half t per year,

00:04:03.395 --> 00:04:04.456
and it starts at ten.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.087
Find the population at time t.

00:04:07.995 --> 00:04:09.043
Think for three seconds.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.753
It asks for a function, so integrate with

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:15.097
plus C, and the start fixes the C.

00:04:16.159 --> 00:04:18.903
Second, find the area between y equals sine

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:21.488
x and the x-axis, from zero to two

00:04:21.529 --> 00:04:21.808
pi.

00:04:22.631 --> 00:04:25.216
The curve crosses the axis at pi, so

00:04:25.317 --> 00:04:25.898
split there.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.027
The integral alone is zero, but the area

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:29.690
is four.

00:04:30.692 --> 00:04:33.076
Third, estimate the integral from zero to one

00:04:33.257 --> 00:04:35.079
of e to the minus x squared.

00:04:35.721 --> 00:04:37.764
This time there's a formula, but it has

00:04:37.905 --> 00:04:39.466
no primitive you can write down in this

00:04:39.528 --> 00:04:41.730
course, so it's the trapezoidal rule again.

00:04:42.662 --> 00:04:44.690
Here's the decision as four short questions.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:45.648
Function?

00:04:46.097 --> 00:04:46.501
Plus C.

00:04:47.213 --> 00:04:47.581
Change?

00:04:48.068 --> 00:04:48.371
Limits.

00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:49.322
Area?

00:04:49.909 --> 00:04:50.193
Split.

00:04:50.841 --> 00:04:51.166
Table?

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:52.156
Trapezia.

00:04:52.821 --> 00:04:55.028
Then look inside the integral for a matched

00:04:55.189 --> 00:04:56.654
inside before you integrate.

00:04:59.514 --> 00:04:59.920
Your turn.

00:05:00.729 --> 00:05:03.134
A tank holds twenty litres at t equals

00:05:03.175 --> 00:05:05.500
zero, and its volume changes at a rate

00:05:05.622 --> 00:05:08.187
of six minus two t litres per minute.

00:05:08.992 --> 00:05:11.131
Find the volume when t equals five.

00:05:12.018 --> 00:05:13.024
Pause here to answer.

00:05:23.668 --> 00:05:25.837
It asks for the volume, so find the

00:05:25.878 --> 00:05:26.198
function.

00:05:26.721 --> 00:05:30.107
V equals six t minus t squared, plus

00:05:30.168 --> 00:05:30.408
C,

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.274
and V of zero is twenty, so C

00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:33.695
is twenty.

00:05:34.638 --> 00:05:38.025
At t equals five, that's thirty, minus twenty-five,

00:05:38.206 --> 00:05:40.370
plus twenty, which is twenty-five litres.

00:05:41.335 --> 00:05:42.562
Five litres is wrong.

00:05:42.764 --> 00:05:45.180
That's the change from zero to five, not

00:05:45.222 --> 00:05:45.664
the volume.

00:05:47.314 --> 00:05:47.741
Last one.

00:05:48.568 --> 00:05:51.449
Find the area bounded by y equals two

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.590
x over x squared plus one, the x-axis,

00:05:54.992 --> 00:05:57.492
and the lines x equals minus one and

00:05:57.693 --> 00:05:58.553
x equals two.

00:05:59.396 --> 00:06:00.483
Pause here to answer.

00:06:11.135 --> 00:06:13.200
The top is the derivative of the bottom,

00:06:13.582 --> 00:06:15.647
so a primitive is the natural log of

00:06:15.688 --> 00:06:17.613
the quantity x squared plus one.

00:06:18.396 --> 00:06:20.540
The curve is below the axis for negative

00:06:20.682 --> 00:06:22.425
x, so split at zero.

00:06:23.229 --> 00:06:26.039
The left piece is minus log two, and

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.645
the right piece is log five.

00:06:28.449 --> 00:06:30.977
Add them as positive amounts: log two plus

00:06:31.018 --> 00:06:33.325
log five is the natural log of ten.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:36.357
Log of five over two is wrong.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.034
It lets the negative piece cancel.

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:42.252
So for any integral question, read what it

00:06:42.514 --> 00:06:45.019
asks for first, then pick the integral.

00:06:45.742 --> 00:06:47.754
Next, the same kind of decision for money

00:06:47.916 --> 00:06:48.619
and chance.

00:06:49.264 --> 00:06:51.471
Here are two investments that differ by just

00:06:51.713 --> 00:06:52.314
one phrase.

00:06:52.958 --> 00:06:55.430
One earns simple interest, and the other is

00:06:55.552 --> 00:06:56.778
compounded annually.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:59.077
Which model does each one need?

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:02.704
Here are the key notes.

00:07:03.347 --> 00:07:05.075
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:05.136 --> 00:07:05.618
to copy them.
